{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having some bloating and changes in your G-tube output?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. My tube output has been brown and sometimes green or yellow. It’s also increased a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you mentioned feeling distended after your last tube feed at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I felt really bloated and uncomfortable. I haven’t had any fever or vomiting, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. No diarrhea either?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of small intestinal bacterial overgrowth and gastric bypass, we’re concerned this could be a recurrence."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. Could the antibiotics I’ve been giving through the tube be affecting it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll hold off on tube feeds for now and start IV fluids to let your bowel rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also start you on IV Zosyn to cover for possible infection while we run some tests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be on that the whole time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2173-01-27 19:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll reassess based on your response. First, we’ll do a plain X-ray to check your bowel gas pattern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2173-01-27 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The KUB came back. Good news — no signs of obstruction or free air. Your G-tube is in place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2173-01-27 20:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2173-01-27 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also do a contrast study tomorrow morning to confirm the tube is functioning properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2173-01-27 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, and what about the bloating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2173-01-27 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting a soap enema every six hours to help relieve distention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. The G-tube study with contrast was successful. The tube is patent and correctly placed in the stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great, so it’s not misplaced?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s where it should be. No leakage either. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the bacteria in the fluid? I saw something about mixed flora."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did see mixed bacterial flora in the fluid sample, but no anaerobes were isolated. It supports the idea of bacterial overgrowth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So is that why the output changed color?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be contributing. We’re switching from IV Zosyn to IV Ceftriaxone and Flagyl to better target gut bacteria."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on Flagyl at home. Should I keep taking it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. You’ll continue oral Flagyl after discharge as part of your treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And can I start eating or using the tube again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to restart your tube feeds slowly and advance your diet to bariatric stage 5 today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve tolerated that before. Should I expect nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2173-01-28 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor closely. You can use ondansetron if needed, but so far you’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2173-01-28 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling this afternoon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2173-01-28 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. The bloating has gone down, and I haven’t had any discomfort with the feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2173-01-28 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Your labs are stable — no fever, normal white count, and lactate is fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2173-01-28 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the blood cultures were negative?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2173-01-28 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, both sets came back with no growth. That rules out a bloodstream infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2173-01-28 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about C. diff? I’ve had it before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2173-01-28 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stool test was negative for C. difficile and other pathogens like Salmonella or Shigella."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2173-01-28 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not infectious diarrhea then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2173-01-28 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it looks like bacterial overgrowth is the main issue, not an acute infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well overnight. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stay on the stage 5 bariatric diet. Don’t advance it on your own. And call the clinic tomorrow to confirm when to restart tube feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I keep taking Flagyl?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue Flagyl 500 mg every 8 hours. We’ve given you a prescription to refill it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I avoid anything else?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Avoid NSAIDs like ibuprofen or naproxen — they can cause ulcers. And no straws or gum to reduce air swallowing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. When should I worry and come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call or return if you get a fever over 101.5, severe pain, vomiting, or can’t eat or drink."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up with my bariatric team?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2173-01-29 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll coordinate your ongoing care. You’re doing well — just keep up the plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2173-01-29 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2173-01-29 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. We'll get your discharge papers ready shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2173-01-29 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check — still no pain, eating well, and moving around okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2173-01-29 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, everything feels back to normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2173-01-29 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Discharge is approved. Take care and follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2173-01-29 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2173-01-29 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in with your discharge instructions and prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2173-01-29 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready when she is."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2173-01-29 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2173-01-27 19:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2173-01-29 14:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for abdominal bloating and changes in gastrostomy tube output, including increased volume and brown or green-yellow discoloration. She has a history of Roux-en-Y gastric bypass, small intestinal bacterial overgrowth, and prior C. difficile. She was managed with NPO status, IV fluids, and IV antibiotics (initially Zosyn, then transitioned to Ceftriaxone and Flagyl). A KUB showed a nonobstructive bowel gas pattern, and a contrast G-tube study confirmed proper placement and patency. Soap enemas were used to relieve distention. By hospital day 2, symptoms improved, she tolerated a bariatric stage 5 diet, and tube feeds were planned for restart at home. She remained afebrile with normal labs and was discharged home on oral Flagyl with follow-up instructions.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications of other bariatric procedure",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Other specified surgical operations and procedures causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Polycystic ovaries",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Personal history of Methicillin resistant Staphylococcus aureus"
    ]
  }
}
